{"ref":"BDB, מֶ֫גֶד","hw":"מֶ֫גֶד","html":"† <big><span dir=\"rtl\">מֶ֫גֶד</span></big>  <strong>n.m. excellence (</strong>NH <em>id.</em>, <em>choice fruit;</em> Syriac <span dir=\"rtl\">ܡܰܓܕܳܐ</span> <em>fruit;</em> Arabic <span dir=\"rtl\">مَجْدٌ</span> <em>glory, honour, nobility</em><strong>)</strong>;—<span dir=\"rtl\">מ׳</span> cstr. <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 33:13\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.33.13\">Dt 33:13</a> + 4 times <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 33\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.33\">Dt 33</a>; pl. <span dir=\"rtl\">מְגָדִים</span> <a data-ref=\"Song of Songs 4:13\" href=\"/Song_of_Songs.4.13\">Ct 4:13</a>; <a data-ref=\"Song of Songs 7:14\" href=\"/Song_of_Songs.7.14\">7:14</a>; sf. <span dir=\"rtl\">מְגָדָיו</span> <a data-ref=\"Song of Songs 4:16\" href=\"/Song_of_Songs.4.16\">Ct 4:16</a>—<em>excellence:</em> excellent or choice things; always of gifts of nature: <span dir=\"rtl\">מ׳ שָׁמַיִם</span> <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 33:13\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.33.13\">Dt 33:13</a> i.e. (natural) gifts of heaven; <span dir=\"rtl\">מ׳ תְּבוּאֹת שֶׁמֶשׁ</span> v <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 33:14\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.33.14\">14</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">מ׳ גֶּרֶשׁ יְרָחִים</span> v <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 33:14\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.33.14\">14</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">מ׳ גִּבְעוֹת עוֹלָם</span> v <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 33:15\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.33.15\">15</a> (‖ <span dir=\"rtl\">רֹאשׁ הַרֲרֵי קֶדֶם</span>); <span dir=\"rtl\">מ׳ אֶרֶץ וּמְלֹאָהּ</span> v <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 33:16\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.33.16\">16</a>; pl. abstr. <span dir=\"rtl\">פְּרִי מ׳</span> (= excellent fruit) <a data-ref=\"Song of Songs 4:13\" href=\"/Song_of_Songs.4.13\">Ct 4:13</a>, <a data-ref=\"Song of Songs 4:16\" href=\"/Song_of_Songs.4.16\">16</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">מ׳</span> alone = foreg., <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 7:14\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.7.14\">7:14</a>.","next":"BDB, מִגְדָּנָה","prev":"BDB, מגד"}